EVALUATION.md §10.5, DECISIONS 398, CHK-05: a package subject names a top-level let of its own package; a const, a fn, a record and a built-in (`len`) or a test local are E5006 notLet.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

const limit = 3

let levels: [Int] = [1]

fn twice(x: Int) -> Int {
  return x + x
}

record Item {
  weight: Int
}

test "not lets" {
  let mine = 1
  expect package { mine: 4 } passes
  expect package { limit: 4 } passes
  expect package { twice: 4 } passes
  expect package { Item: 4 } passes
  expect package { len: 4, min: 1 } passes
  expect package { levels: [2] } passes
}
-- findings.txt --
warning[W1002]  a/a.canon:11:8
  record Item has no doc comment

warning[W1002]  a/a.canon:12:3
  field weight has no doc comment

error[E5006]  a/a.canon:17:20
  mine is not a let: expect package substitutes top-level lets of its own package

error[E5006]  a/a.canon:18:20
  limit is not a let: expect package substitutes top-level lets of its own package

error[E5006]  a/a.canon:19:20
  twice is not a let: expect package substitutes top-level lets of its own package

error[E5006]  a/a.canon:20:20
  Item is not a let: expect package substitutes top-level lets of its own package

error[E5006]  a/a.canon:21:20
  len is not a let: expect package substitutes top-level lets of its own package

error[E5006]  a/a.canon:21:28
  min is not a let: expect package substitutes top-level lets of its own package

6 errors, 2 warnings in 1 package (…)
